Sorry for the thread resurrection but I delved a bit into the source
of SLASHEM to look what could have happened. The answer is simple:

A magic lamp generated in the black market is always empty.
(source: shknam.c 715
	  if (typ==MAGIC_LAMP) {
	    otmp->spe = 0;
	  }
)

I also found some other things regarding magic lamps, but these are
*SPOILERS*! scroll down to see.













According to the source, magic lamps cannot be cancelled. Only if they
are wished for they are set to have no oil. I searched the source
files, and only found one place which said that it was out of oil.
(code links below

Source files:
zap.c line 969:
	    if (obj->spe != ((obj->oclass == WAND_CLASS) ? -1 : 0) &&
	       obj->otyp != WAN_CANCELLATION &&
		 /* can't cancel cancellation */
		 obj->otyp != MAGIC_LAMP &&
		 obj->otyp != MAGIC_CANDLE &&
		 obj->otyp != CANDELABRUM_OF_INVOCATION) {
		costly_cancel(obj);
		obj->spe = (obj->oclass == WAND_CLASS) ? -1 : 0;
	    }
apply.c line 1160
	/* magic lamps with an spe == 0 (wished for) cannot be lit */
	if ((!Is_candle(obj) && obj->age == 0)
			|| (obj->otyp == MAGIC_LAMP && obj->spe == 0)) {
		if ((obj->otyp == BRASS_LANTERN)
#ifdef LIGHTSABERS
			|| is_lightsaber(obj)
#endif
			)
			Your("%s has run out of power.", xname(obj));
		else if (obj->otyp == TORCH) {
		        Your("torch has burnt out and cannot be relit.");
		}
		else pline("This %s has no oil.", xname(obj));
		return;
	}


A magic lamp can become a normal oil lamp if you dip it in Lethe.
A charging unpaid magic lamp in a shop has the same cost as charging a
normal lamp. But this does nothing to the lamp. (Greedy bastard
shopkeepers).
potion.c 3033:  /* Adding oil to an empty magic lamp renders it into
an oil lamp */
Dipping a magic lamp in a potion of amnesia makes it a oil lamp

